## 🚀 **Installation Commands**

### **Main Installer**
```bash
# One-line installation
curl -sSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yourusername/easyinstall/main/easyinstall.sh | sudo bash

# Run installer manually
sudo ./easyinstall.sh

# Check installation status
easyinstall status
```

---

## 🌐 **WordPress Commands**

### **Traditional WordPress (Separate Redis per site)**
```bash
# Basic installation
easyinstall wp example.com

# With specific PHP version
easyinstall wp example.com --php=8.3
easyinstall wp example.com --php=8.2
easyinstall wp example.com --php=8.1

# With SSL
easyinstall wp example.com --ssl

# With custom options
easyinstall wp example.com --php=8.3 --ssl

# Multiple sites (each gets unique Redis port)
easyinstall wp site1.com      # Redis port: 6379
easyinstall wp site2.com      # Redis port: 6380
easyinstall wp site3.com      # Redis port: 6381
```

### **WordPress with Docker**
```bash
# Basic Docker installation
easyinstall wp-docker example.com

# With specific PHP version
easyinstall wp-docker example.com --php=8.3

# With specific MySQL version
easyinstall wp-docker example.com --mysql=8.0
easyinstall wp-docker example.com --mysql=5.7

# With SSL
easyinstall wp-docker example.com --ssl

# Full options
easyinstall wp-docker example.com --php=8.3 --mysql=8.0 --ssl

# Multiple Docker sites (each gets unique port)
easyinstall wp-docker site1.com      # Port: 8080
easyinstall wp-docker site2.com      # Port: 8081
easyinstall wp-docker site3.com      # Port: 8082
```

### **Aliases**
```bash
# WordPress aliases
easyinstall wordpress example.com    # Same as 'wp'
easyinstall docker-wp example.com    # Same as 'wp-docker'
```

