## ⚡ **Redis Management**

### **Redis Status & Information**
```bash
# Show all Redis instances
easyinstall redis-status

# List all Redis ports in use
easyinstall redis-ports

# Show Redis memory usage
redis-cli -p 6379 INFO memory | grep used_memory_human

# Monitor Redis commands
redis-cli -p 6379 MONITOR
```

### **Redis Instance Management**
```bash
# Restart Redis for a specific site
easyinstall redis-restart example.com

# Stop Redis for a site
sudo systemctl stop redis-example-com

# Start Redis for a site
sudo systemctl start redis-example-com

# Check Redis logs
journalctl -u redis-example-com -f
```

### **Redis CLI Access**
```bash
# Access Redis CLI for a specific site
easyinstall redis-cli example.com

# Then use Redis commands:
redis 127.0.0.1:6379> ping
redis 127.0.0.1:6379> info keyspace
redis 127.0.0.1:6379> dbsize
redis 127.0.0.1:6379> flushall  # Clear all cache (caution!)
```

### **Redis Configuration**
```bash
# View Redis config
cat /etc/redis/redis-example-com.conf

# Edit Redis config
nano /etc/redis/redis-example-com.conf

# After editing, restart
systemctl restart redis-example-com
```

