## 🐳 **Docker Management**

### **Docker Site Operations**
```bash
# List all Docker sites
easyinstall docker-list

# Show Docker ports in use
easyinstall docker-ports

# Start a Docker site
easyinstall docker-start example.com

# Stop a Docker site
easyinstall docker-stop example.com

# Restart a Docker site
easyinstall docker-restart example.com

# View Docker logs
easyinstall docker-logs example.com
easyinstall docker-logs example.com nginx     # Specific container
easyinstall docker-logs example.com wordpress
easyinstall docker-logs example.com db
easyinstall docker-logs example.com redis
```

### **Docker Container Access**
```bash
# Shell into WordPress container
easyinstall docker-shell example.com
easyinstall docker-shell example.com wordpress

# Shell into database container
easyinstall docker-shell example.com db

# Shell into Redis container
easyinstall docker-shell example.com redis

# Shell into Nginx container
easyinstall docker-shell example.com nginx
```

### **Docker Redis Access**
```bash
# Redis CLI for Docker site
easyinstall docker-redis example.com

# Then use Redis commands inside container
```

### **Docker Compose Commands**
```bash
# Go to site directory
cd /var/lib/docker-sites/wordpress/example.com

# Custom docker-compose commands
docker-compose ps                    # List containers
docker-compose top                   # Show processes
docker-compose logs -f                # Follow logs
docker-compose exec wordpress bash    # Shell access
docker-compose restart                 # Restart all
docker-compose down                     # Stop and remove
docker-compose up -d                     # Start again
```

